   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How… / how much…",
     "texto": [
      "**얼마나 + adjective + -(으)ㄴ지 모르다** can emphasise a degree: **얼마나 좋은지 몰라요** = you can't imagine how good it is. It does not always literally mean that someone does not know something.",
      "With verbs, use **얼마나 + -는지 모르다**: 얼마나 기다리는지 몰라요 = you can't imagine how long (he/she) waits."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Indirect question",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)ㄴ지** also introduces an indirect question with adjectives: 좋은지 알아요? = do you know whether it is good? **몰라요** means «I don't know» and **모르겠어요**, depending on the context, «I don't know / I'm not sure»; one does not always express more certainty than the other.",
      "The context helps tell an indirect question apart from the emphatic use of **얼마나**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
